That does make things easier. Several whole lines or
fractions of lines would work, yet remain
wonderfully obscure.

        It will never be broken by Maud,
        she has neither savour nor salt

        Ah Maud, you milkwhite fawn,
        you are all unmeet for a wife.

        Whom but Maud should I meet?

This one (above) looks useful.

        Maud could be gracious too, no doubt

        If Maud were all that she seem'd

        Maud, Maud, Maud, Maud,
        They were crying and calling.

The above could be interpreted as someone trying to
remind the PC just who that Maud person is.

        Maud is here, here, here
        In among the lilies.

        Maud is as true as Maud is sweet

This one above works wonderfully as sarcasm in the
game context.

        Make answer, Maud my bliss

        For shall not Maud have her will?

That last one is certainly my favorite for the case
where the unIDed =oMemory is thwarting the
?oAmnesia.

